+++ b/cmake/BusterStartOrder.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,678 @@
+# The functions small compiles run, in the order the link places them before .text (#1444): `UNIT NAME` for a
+# function of one of main.c's units, placed by its unit's object and its section, and `- NAME` for one of the C
+# library's, placed by its name (cmake/BusterStartOrder.cmake, docs/commands/build.md, "The start's code order").
+#
+# Written by `compiler start-order` from main at b7a95eedb, built on the 9700X as the benchmark builds are
+# (BUSTER_HOST_ARCH=znver5 BUSTER_DEBUG_INFO=0, Release, clang 23.1.1, lld 23), placement 0 of `build.sh shifts`: its
+# `readelf -sW`, and `perf record -b -e instructions:u -c 4999` of an empty file's -fsyntax-only (300 processes) and
+# -E -P, tiny.c's -c and hello.c's -c (200 processes each; the inputs of buster-performance's
+# docs/measurements/start-order-1444-2026-11-13). Refresh it as that guide says when small compiles' code moves.
+# start-order: 5294065 addresses, 413804 of them in no function; 482 local functions of main.c's units (2634 KB) and 186 by name (99 KB)
